=== 2. Finding V1 (BLOCKING): false Verified on any claim that is wrong only for x < 0
verify_equivalence builds its pool in region order: 15 points in [0.2, 4.0],
15 in [0.05, 0.95], 15 in [1.0, 8.0], 15 in [-4.0, -0.2], 15 in [-3.0, 3.0],
then 10 fixed points (0.37 .. 3.0, all positive). It stops at
TARGET_SAMPLE_POINTS = 16 accepted points. If no point is skipped, the 16
points are the 15 of [0.2, 4.0] plus the first of [0.05, 0.95]. The negative
regions are reached only when points are skipped. So a claim that is right for
x > 0 and wrong for x < 0 is Verified. Probes (extra.rs probes(), Appendix B),
output verbatim:
identity      x                      == abs(x)                     vars ["x"]: Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 0.0 } }
identity      x                      == sqrt(x ^ 2)                vars ["x"]: Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 0.0 } }
identity      x ^ 3                  == abs(x) ^ 3                 vars ["x"]: Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 0.0 } }
identity      sin(x)                 == sin(abs(x))                vars ["x"]: Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 0.0 } }
identity      x * y                  == abs(x) * abs(y)            vars ["x", "y"]: Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 0.0 } }
integral      d/dx[x ^ 2 / 2] == abs(x): Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 0.0 } }
integral      d/dx[x * abs(x) / 2] == x: Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 0.0 } }
factorisation x ^ 3 - x == ["abs(x)", "x - 1", "x + 1"]: Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: 16, max_relative_error: 2.0520894020146044e-16 } }
identity      x                      == x + 0.001                  vars ["x"]: Failed { counterexample: {"x": 0.24988183567014408}, expected: 0.25088183567014405, got: 0.24988183567014408 }
test extra 4 ... ok
result: 1 passed; 0 failed

8 of 8 false claims are Verified; the control (wrong for positive x) fails.
"x == abs(x)" and "d/dx[x^2/2] == abs(x)" are false. The work order says "A
false Verified is a project-stopping bug." Every Verified in the corpus, and in
the card store later, rests on this sampler.
Fix direction (author's choice): shuffle the pool, or take points round-robin
from every region, so that no region is skipped by the stop at 16. Then add
these 8 probes as tests that must return Failed. The mutation operators cannot
find this class: none of them produces abs() from x, so the mutation test is
blind to it by construction (see V3).

